findings.body:
The level is set by assigning to the attribute and calling `save!`, instead of going through `TopicUser.change`. That skips three things `change` does:
- setting `notifications_changed_at` and `notifications_reason_id` (user_changed);
- publishing `notification_level_change` on MessageBus;
- the observer callbacks.

As a result, other open clients do not see the new level. Also, the reason is never recorded, so auto-tracking logic that checks `notifications_reason_id IS NULL` (e.g. `update_last_read`, `auto_track`) can bump the topic back to tracking later, silently undoing the unsubscribe.
